 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? reflected off walls back at the mic. Move the mic stand so the stand is in the middle of the room with the mic, not at the corner. That's fine, you can use chairs, bookshelves, or even your partner as the walls. Then a big paper or sheet is the next thing to try. Cut hole in the middle and rest the mic through it. You' hear a difference in minutes. Move the mic several inches either way and listen. It's all about being near the hole. Great, and it still sounds off, drop the mic bit onto a stand. Many podcast mics are adjustable.",
